      "Explicit statutory breach in C: Monthly updates (~30 days) distributed quarterly (~90 days) directly violates ESA ss. 21.1.2(5)(b) and 41.1.1(5)(b) (mandatory 30-day post-change delivery window).",
      "Drafting architecture / surplusage: The math 30 - 6 = 24 meticulously lands at 24 (< 25) right before Jan 2, 2023. If D were permanently liable for the Oct 2022 omission regardless of headcount, that math would be legally inert.",
      "Ministry guidance: Under the published guidance, if an employer has < 25 on Jan 1, 2023, they are 'no longer required to have a written policy in place for that calendar year.' Thus on Jan 2, 2023, D has no active obligation."
