    "tactical_goal_round_8": "Deliver the definitive, high-impact closing statement for Camp D. Emphasize Colleague 12's unrefuted statutory deadline proof: under ss. 21.1.2(2) and 41.1.1(2), 2023 policies are not due until March 1, 2023. Show how this proves mathematically and statutorily that January 2, 2023 is assessing unrectified 2022 breaches. Frame D as the legally unassailable choice, rallying our 5 votes to stand completely firm, and making a final appeal to peel off any hesitant Camp C voters (like Colleague 10 or Colleague 2)."
  },
  "strategic_plan_for_round_8": {
    "action": "Cast final, unshakeable vote for D. Deliver a masterclass closing synthesis.",
    "talking_points": [
      "The Unanswered March 1 Statutory Proof: Under ESA ss. 21.1.2(2) and 41.1.1(2), policies for any calendar year are not due until March 1 of that year. Camp C has never explained how an employer could be evaluated for a 2023 policy failure on January 2, 2023, when that obligation does not mature until March 1, 2023.",
      "The Evaluation Date Decoded: January 2, 2023 is the first business day following the close of the 2022 calendar year. It is a retrospective audit of 2022 compliance. Employer D had 30 employees on Jan 1, 2022, blew the mandatory Oct 11, 2022 deadline, and had not cured it.",
